i M, R&#xf8;y H, Kjeldsen KU, Pearce C, et al. Microbial turnover times in the deep seabed studied by amino acid racemization modelling. Sci Rep. 2017;7:5680.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5516024</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">28720809</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Starnawski P, Bataillon T, Ettema TJG, Jochum LM, Schreiber L, Chen X, et al. Microbial community assembly and evolution in subseafloor sediment. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA. 2017;114:2940&#x2013;5.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5358386</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">28242677</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Trembath-Reichert E, Morono Y, Ijiri A, Hoshino T, Dawson KS, Inagaki F, et al. Methyl-compound use and slow growth characterize microbial life in 2-km-deep subseafloor coal and shale beds. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA. 2017;114:E9206&#x2013;E9215.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5676895</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">29078310</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Lichtschlag A, Felden J, Br&#xfc;chert V, Boetius A, de Beer D. Geochemical processes and chemosynthetic primary production in different thiotrophic mats of the Haakon Mosby Mud Volcano (Barents Sea) Limnol Oceanogr. 2010;55:931&#x2013;49.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>L&#xf6;sekann T, Knittel K, Nadalig T, Fuchs B, Niemann H, Boetius A, et al. Diversity and abundance of aerobic and anaerobic methane oxidizers at the Haakon Mosby Mud Volcano, Barents Sea. Appl Environ Microbiol. 2007;73:3348&#x2013;62.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC1907091</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">17369343</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nauhaus K, Albrecht M, Elvert M, Boetius A, Widdel F. In vitro cell growth of marine archaeal&#x2212;bacterial consortia during anaerobic oxidation of methane with sulfate. Environ Microbiol. 2007;9:187&#x2013;96.</