Microbiol. 1992 Aug;58(8):2663-6</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">1514813</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Science. 2008 Feb 1;319(5863):604-7</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18239121</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nature. 2007 Oct 18;449(7164):898-901</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">17882164</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Microbiol Rep. 2009 Oct;1(5):370-6</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">23765889</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Appl Environ Microbiol. 1996 Oct;62(10):3605-13</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">8837415</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Appl Environ Microbiol. 2008 May;74(10):3022-9</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18378655</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Biotechnol Bioeng. 2010 Feb 15;105(3):524-33</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">19787639</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nature. 1994 Dec 1;372(6505):455-8</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">7984238</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Microbiol. 2012 Oct;14(10):2726-40</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">22827909</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Pollut. 2005 Jan;133(1):71-84</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">15327858</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>PLoS One. 2014 Aug 20;9(8):e105356</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">25141130</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>ISME J. 2015 Sep;9(9):2028-45</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">25734684</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Appl Environ Microbiol. 2008 Jan;74(1):286-93</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">17981943</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Microbiol. 2007 Jan;9(1):187-96</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">17227423</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nature. 2015 Oct 22;526(7574):531-5</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26375009</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Appl Environ Microbiol. 2003 Jan;69(1):434-43</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">12514025</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Microbiol Rev. 1995 Jun;59(2):201-22</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">7603409</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Appl Environ Microbiol. 1977 Feb;33(2):254-6</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">192144</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>J Appl Bacteriol. 1977 Aug;43(1):1-24</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">332677</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Microbiol. 2010 Nov;12(11):3074-86</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">20602630</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Front Microbiol. 2015 Feb 20;6:116</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">25806023</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Microbiol. 2002 May;4(5):296-305</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">12080959</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nature. 1999 Sep 16;401(6750):266-9</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">10499582</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Biotechnol Bioeng. 2009 Oct 15;104(3):458-70</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">19544305</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Front Microbiol. 2016 Feb 18;7:75</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26925032</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Talanta. 1999 Feb;48(2):347-53</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">18967472</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>ISME J. 2014 Oct;8(10):2029-44</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24722631</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Microbiol. 2014 Jan;16(1):130-40</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24028539</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Appl Environ Microbiol. 2005 Jul;71(7):3725-33</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">16000782</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nature. 2016 Nov 17;539(7629):396-401</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27749816</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nature. 2000 Oct 5;407(6804):623-6</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">11034209</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Front Microbiol. 2016 Feb 02;7:46</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26870011</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Environ Microbiol. 2009 Dec;11(12):3223-32</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">19703218</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference></ReferenceList></PubmedData></PubmedArticle><PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation Status="MEDLINE" Owner="NLM" IndexingMethod="Manual"><PMID Version="1">29769540</PMID><DateCompleted><Year>2019</Year><Month>11</Month><Day>19</Day></DateCompleted><DateRevised><Year>2019</Year><Month>11</Month><Day>19</Day></DateRevised><Article PubModel="Electronic"><Journal><ISSN IssnType="Electronic">2045-2322</ISSN><JournalIssue CitedMedium="Internet"><Volume>8</Volume><Issue>1</Issue><PubDate><Year>2018</Year><Month>May</Month><Day>16</Day></PubDate></JournalIssue><Title>Scientific reports</Title><ISOAbbreviation>Sci Rep</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>Different clusters of Candidatus 'Methanoperedens nitroreducens'-like archaea as revealed by high-throughput sequencing with new primers.</ArticleTitle><Pagination><StartPage>7695</StartPage><MedlinePgn>7695</MedlinePgn></Pagination><ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">7695</ELocationID><ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/s41598-018-24974-z</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText>The newly discovered Candidatus 'Methanoperedens nitroreducens' (M. nitroreducens), mediating nitrate-dependent anaerobic oxidation of methane, is an important microorganism in linking carbon and nitrogen cycles. In order to explore the diversity of M. nitroreducens-like archaea in various environmental niches with advanced high-throughput sequencing, new primers based on alpha subunit of methyl-coenzyme M reductase gene were designed. The PCR results demonstrated that the new primers could effectively detect M. nitroreducens-like archaea from an enrichment culture dominated by M. nitroreducens as well as samples collected from a natural freshwater lake and a full-scale wastewater treatment plant (WWTP). By high-throughput sequencing, more than 30,000 M. nitroreducens-like sequences were obtained. Phylogenetic analysis of these sequences along with published sequences showed that M. nitroreducens-like archaea could be divided into three sub-branches (named as Group A, Group B and Group C in this study). Clear geographical difference was observed, with Group A and Group B dominating samples in Queensland (Australia) and in European ecosystems, respectively. Further quantitative PCR revealed that the M. nitroreducens-like archaea were more abundant in WWTP than the freshwater lake. The study provided a large number of sequences for M. nitroreducens-like archaeal communities, thus expanded our understanding on the ecological diversity of M. nitroreducens-like archaea.</AbstractText></Abstract><AuthorList CompleteYN="Y"><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Xu</LastName><ForeName>Sai</ForeName><Initials>S</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Advanced Water Management Centre, The University of Queensland, Brisbane, 4072, Australia.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>School of Environment, Tsinghua University, Beijing, 100084, China.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Key Laboratory for Solid Waste Management and Environment Safety (Tsinghua University), Ministry of Education of China, Tsinghua University, Beijing, 100084, China.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Cai</LastName><ForeName>Chen</ForeName><Initials>C</Initials><Identifier Source="ORCID">0000-0002-0167-1397</Identifier><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Advanced Water Management Centre, The University of Queensland, Brisbane, 4072, Australia.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Guo</LastName><ForeName>Jianhua</ForeName><Initials>J</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Advanced Water Management Centre, The University of Queensland, Brisbane, 4072, Australia.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Lu</LastName><ForeName>Wenjing</ForeName><Initials>W</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>School of Environment, Tsinghua University, Beijing, 100084, China. luwenjing@tsinghua.edu.cn.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Key Laboratory for Solid Waste Management and Environment Safety (Tsinghua University), Ministry of Education of China, Tsinghua University, Beijing, 100084, China. luwenjing@tsinghua.edu.cn.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Yuan</LastName><ForeName>Zhiguo</ForeName><Initials>Z</Initials><Identifier Source="ORCID">0000-0002-7566-1482</Identifier><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Advanced Water Management Centre, The University of Queensland, Brisbane, 4072, Australia.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>School of Environment, Tsinghua University, Beijing, 100084, China.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN="Y"><LastName>Hu</LastName><ForeName>Shihu</ForeName><Initials>S</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Advanced Water Management Centre, The University of Queensland, Brisbane, 4072, Australia. s.hu@awmc.uq.edu.au.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author></AuthorList><Language>eng</Language><PublicationTypeList><PublicationType UI="D016428">Journal Article</PublicationType><PublicationType UI="D013485">Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't</PublicationType></PublicationTypeList><ArticleDate DateType="Electronic"><Year>2018</Year><Month>05</Month><Day>16</Day></ArticleDate></Article><MedlineJournalInfo><Country>England</Country><MedlineTA>Sci Rep</MedlineTA><NlmUniqueID>101563288</NlmUniqueID><ISSNLinking>2045-2322</ISSNLinking></MedlineJournalInfo><ChemicalList><Chemical><RegistryNumber>0</RegistryNumber><NameOfSubstance UI="D017931">DNA Primers</NameOfSubstance></Chemical><Chemical><RegistryNumber>0</RegistryNumber><NameOfSubstance UI="D019641">DNA, Archaeal</NameOfSubstance></Chemical></ChemicalList><CitationSubset>IM</CitationSubset><MeshHeadingList><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D044822" MajorTopicYN="N">Biodiversity</DescriptorName></MeshHeading><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D017931" MajorTopicYN="N">DNA Primers</DescriptorName><QualifierName UI="Q000737" MajorTopicYN="Y">chemistry</QualifierName></MeshHeading><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D019641" MajorTopicYN="N">DNA, Archaeal</DescriptorName><QualifierName UI="Q000032" MajorTopicYN="Y">analysis</QualifierName><QualifierName UI="Q000235" MajorTopicYN="N">genetics</QualifierName></MeshHeading><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D017753" MajorTopicYN="N">Ecosystem</DescriptorName></MeshHeading><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D059014" MajorTopicYN="N">High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing</DescriptorName><QualifierName UI="Q000379" MajorTopicYN="Y">methods</QualifierName></MeshHeading><MeshHeading><DescriptorName UI="D019640" MajorTopicYN="N">Methanosarcinales</DescriptorName><QualifierName UI="Q000145" MajorTopicYN="Y">clas